WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.510
Film Courage: When you’re writing a screenplay
do you start with an outline?

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.660
Rachel K. Ofori, Producer/Writer: I start
with somewhat of an outline.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.769
I need to know where I am and then where I
am going or where I just came from.

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:16.890
Usually for me when I am starting to write
it’s not coming from a starting place, it’s

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.400
coming from a scene I’ve already had so
I write that scene out, the most vivid thing

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.000
about what I think about this idea, I write
that scene out any…it doesn’t have to

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.000
fit anywhere.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.670
I don’t know where this is but I just see
these characters doing this at some point.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.860
I start there because I kind of get my groove
going and I start to…yeah I really feel

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:34.860
this moment.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.860
I see this moment.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.930
I’m a very visual writer.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.330
When ideas come to me they come to me almost
like a movie.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.690
I’m able to write them down and then now
I go to an outline because I don’t even

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.690
know where this is.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:01:28.160
I know I am here 

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:57.370
but I don’t even 

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:33.260
know where this 
is in 

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.280
the story

